{
  "id": 459978950,
  "iid": 23732,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "Eliminate a few Coverity null pointer check warnings",
  "description": "In the SMB dissector, pdata was always allocated immediately above\nif it didn't exist, so we don't need the checks (and it's always\ndereferenced before the checks.) Also fix a complaint about\nleft-shifting a max value uint16_t by 16 after the integer promotions\nconvert to a signed int.\n\nIn the WPS dissector, we don't need to check NULL before calling\nproto_item_append_text, which does NULL checking for us. The\npacket_info struct is never NULL when a dissector is called\n(and it gets deferenced later anyway by dissect_wps_tlvs), so\nwe don't need that check either.\n\nIn dumpcap, the capture opts should never set output_to_pipe to\ntrue while setting saving_to_file to false.\n\nCoverity CIDs 1666656, 1604224, 1660860, 1641423\n\nAI-Assisted: no",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2026-02-28T23:05:52.908Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-03-01T04:03:36.484Z",
